<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christian I of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1426">1426</a>–<a href="/years/1481">1481</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-oldenburg">House of Oldenburg</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christian I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> was the first king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-oldenburg">House of Oldenburg</a>, elected in Denmark in 1448 and later king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and, briefly, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. In 1460 the estates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> and Holstein elected him their ruler under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ribe">Treaty of Ribe</a>, promising the lands would stay forever undivided. He founded the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> in 1479.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christian-i-of-denmark.jpg" alt="Christian I of Denmark" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christian_I_of_Denmark,_Norway_%26_Sweden_1440s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>On a ridge outside Stockholm, the Swedish regent Sten Sture the Elder, with peasants, miners and burghers, defeated King <b>Christian I of Denmark</b>, who sought to enforce his rule over Sweden under the Kalmar Union.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-10">10 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The Rendsburg line died out in 1459, and the estates of Schleswig and Holstein chose <b>King Christian I of Denmark</b> as ruler in 1460 under the Treaty of Ribe.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-holstein">County of Holstein</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1448 Count <b>Christian of Oldenburg</b> was elected King of Denmark as Christian I, founding the House of Oldenburg, which later ruled Denmark, Norway, Sweden, Russia and Greece in its various branches.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-oldenburg">County of Oldenburg</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1460 the estates of the Duchy of Schleswig and the County of Holstein elected <b>King Christian I of Denmark</b> as their ruler, promising that the lands would remain 'forever undivided'.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-holstein">Duchy of Holstein</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Oldenburg, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. Died in Copenhagen Castle, in what is now <a href="/countries/denmark">Denmark</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=53.14,8.21&amp;year=1461" aria-label="Oldenburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4733 334 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Christian I of Denmark"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5183 604h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5183 604h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=53.14,8.21&amp;year=1461">What was here in 1461? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
